# TASTE.md -- scars

Rulings this project actually made. Each carries its why; a scar
without a why is a ban, and bans fossilize. Read this before any
design verdict; delete a scar the moment its expiry condition
arrives. Material lives in DESIGN.md.

This file starts empty and stays empty until something real is
rejected here. Structural priors that hold on almost every product
ship with the skill (`references/priors.md` in design-skill); read
them at Review, do not copy them into this file. A scar is earned
when a change on this project is rejected on evidence -- record it
in this form and keep the whole entry under ten lines:

## {DATE} rejected: {what was rejected, one line}

Why: {the failure, concretely -- what task got harder, what broke,
what it read as}
Where: {the surface, run, or capture that shows it}
Landed: {the narrowest layer that now enforces the correction --
DESIGN.md prose, a token, a component, a check -- or "nowhere yet"}
Reuse: {the rule going forward, one or two lines}
Expires: {never (structural | perceptual | behavioral | voice), or
the condition that retires it}
